# Character expressions are data. Playback and inspection choose a pose;
# both use the same painter over the production artwork.
import lib/std.dl

class:
    patterns:
        website river expression pose
    members:
        left blink as an integer
        right blink as an integer
        mouth as a floating-point number
        licking as a boolean
        tongue phase as a floating-point number

class:
    patterns:
        website river blink timing
    members:
        duration as a floating-point number
        offset as a floating-point number

the website river blink timings means: [
    @intrinsic("construct", website river blink timing, 7.3, 0.0),
    @intrinsic("construct", website river blink timing, 6.4, 2.1),
    @intrinsic("construct", website river blink timing, 8.1, 4.6),
    @intrinsic("construct", website river blink timing, 1.0, 0.0)
]

to get the website river blink timing for {integer:subject}:
    return the item at subject in (the website river blink timings)

class:
    patterns:
        website river eye overlay
    members:
        subject as an integer
        side as an integer
        sprite as an integer
        horizontal offset as a floating-point number
        vertical offset as a floating-point number
        x as a floating-point number
        y as a floating-point number
        horizontal radius as a floating-point number
        vertical radius as a floating-point number
        solid as a floating-point number

a river eye for {integer:subject} side {integer:side} using sprite {integer:sprite} shifted {floating-point number:horizontal} {floating-point number:vertical} centered {floating-point number:x} {floating-point number:y} radius {floating-point number:rx} {floating-point number:ry} solid {floating-point number:solid} means: @intrinsic("construct", website river eye overlay, subject, side, sprite, horizontal, vertical, x, y, rx, ry, solid)

the website river eye overlays means: [
    a river eye for 0 side 0 using sprite 5 shifted 0.0 0.0 centered 0.36 0.35 radius 0.09 0.15 solid (0.55 / 0.78),
    a river eye for 1 side 0 using sprite 6 shifted 0.0 -0.03 centered 0.455 0.44 radius 0.09 0.09 solid 0.8,
    a river eye for 1 side 1 using sprite 6 shifted 0.0 -0.03 centered 0.68 0.44 radius 0.09 0.09 solid 0.8,
    a river eye for 2 side 0 using sprite 7 shifted 0.0 0.0 centered 0.364 0.504 radius 0.08 0.075 solid 0.82,
    a river eye for 2 side 1 using sprite 7 shifted -0.018 0.012 centered 0.559 0.49 radius 0.08 0.075 solid 0.82
]

to get the website river blink at {floating-point number:seconds} cycling {floating-point number:duration} offset {floating-point number:offset}:
    set phase to (seconds + offset) / duration
    set phase to phase - (the floor of phase)
    if (phase <= 0.91) or (phase >= 0.95):
        return 0
    if phase < 0.92:
        return ((phase - 0.91) * 25500.0) as an integer
    if phase > 0.94:
        return ((0.95 - phase) * 25500.0) as an integer
    return 255

to get the website river expression for {integer:subject} at {floating-point number:seconds}:
    set pose to a new website river expression pose
    set blink to 0
    if subject < 3:
        set timing to the website river blink timing for subject
        set blink to the website river blink at seconds cycling (timing's duration) offset (timing's offset)
    set pose's left blink and pose's right blink to blink
    return pose
